{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1167070-odd-lunar-concepts","id":1167070,"title":"Odd Lunar Concepts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-12T12:18:55-08:00","id":1167070,"title":"Odd Lunar Concepts","content":"So most of the time, Lunars are typified by having big, badass animal totems, or else ones that you see all the time in fiction.<br /> <br /> This thread is not necessarily for those Lunars.<br /> <br /> I'm gonna name some animals; what character concepts do you think would work for a Lunar with that animal as their spirit shape? I'm interested to see what people come up with.<br /> <br /> Ready?<br /> <br /> Your first few animals are: mountain goat, anaconda, locust, and shrike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Teller of Tales, and the Weaver of Dreams<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14qUE6JyfwtXyd8SMY5gSJ_vvUZPCvGDZiIbBk19QPiU/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Behold! My 2e characters.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13327-voyd211","name":"Voyd211","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13327_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T12:23:57-08:00","id":1167074,"title":"","content":"Goat makes me think of a no moon sorcerer, with a long beard, curving horns and hooves, and a number of summoned demons to do his cackling bidding.<br /> <br /> Shrike? A butcher. Both literally and metaphorically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T12:25:38-08:00","id":1167076,"title":"","content":"Mountain Goat is a mountain hermit. Im reminded of that weird translation error, where artists thought Moses had horns for a bit. If they have beastmen, its gonna be a sheer cliff face and hard to scale. Id kinda want to see them as a Baphomet looking guy, or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T12:31:06-08:00","id":1167079,"title":"","content":"An anaconda lunar would not wanr none unless you've got buns, hun.....<br /> <br /> <br /> i'll show myself out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T12:46:07-08:00","id":1167088,"title":"","content":"I've got several more groups, but I'll only post another when all four animals from the previous list have been used.<br /> <br /> Meaning: y'all still got an overgrown grasshopper to work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Teller of Tales, and the Weaver of Dreams<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14qUE6JyfwtXyd8SMY5gSJ_vvUZPCvGDZiIbBk19QPiU/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Behold! My 2e characters.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13327-voyd211","name":"Voyd211","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13327_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T12:48:59-08:00","id":1167091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voyd211</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1167070-odd-lunar-concepts?p=1167088#post1167088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got several more groups, but I'll only post another when all four animals from the previous list have been used.<br /> <br /> Meaning: y'all still got an overgrown grasshopper to work with.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not even really a challenge. Locusts, especially if they're large enough to qualify as even a small Lunar totem, are ravenous destroyers of crops and vegetation. The character could be driving the Realm off with appetite alone, since it can't gain a foothold where it can't trust its food supplies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T12:53:03-08:00","id":1167095,"title":"","content":"I imagine that if you're building an advanced Essence 4+ Lunar, then you could use Emerald Grasshopper Form for insect totems.<br /> <br /> Next group!<br /> <br /> Robber fly, poison dart frog, koi, and giant tortoise.<br /> <br /> I'll be amazed if anyone knows that first one without looking it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Teller of Tales, and the Weaver of Dreams<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14qUE6JyfwtXyd8SMY5gSJ_vvUZPCvGDZiIbBk19QPiU/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Behold! My 2e characters.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13327-voyd211","name":"Voyd211","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13327_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T19:42:48-08:00","id":1167203,"title":"","content":"Anaconda practically screams a master wrestler, probably female since they're bigger and stronger than the males. Either way, not ashamed of jumping an opponent from behind, unless their honor and title are at stake.<br /> <br /> Poison Dart Frog is a good one for a Changing Moon assassin who hides in plain sight, distracting their target with a flashy appearance, so they never know they've been murdered until it's too late.<br /> <br /> Giant Tortoise sounds fun, similar to the snapping turtle totem I did once, only less aggressive. A defensive warrior, who stands between his friends and the enemy clad in the heaviest moonsilver armor and shield he can get, outlasting them with sheer endurance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T20:10:31-08:00","id":1167208,"title":"","content":"...yanno what, SCREW IT. Have all the animals!<br /> <br /> Robber fly, poison dart frog, koi, tortoise<br /> <br /> Firefly, jellyfish, goose, walrus<br /> <br /> Porcupine, cuttlefish, hellbender, heron<br /> <br /> Pelican, catfish, starfish, flying fox<br /> <br /> Sea turtle, beaded lizard, gharial, rattlesnake<br /> <br /> Lionfish, archer fish, sailfish, deep-sea angler<br /> <br /> Lobster, velvet worm, weaver spider, centipede<br /> <br /> Mantis, cicada, stag beetle, bee<br /> <br /> I'll throw more in here when I come up with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Teller of Tales, and the Weaver of Dreams<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14qUE6JyfwtXyd8SMY5gSJ_vvUZPCvGDZiIbBk19QPiU/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Behold! My 2e characters.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13327-voyd211","name":"Voyd211","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13327_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T21:40:52-08:00","id":1167220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voyd211</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1167070-odd-lunar-concepts?p=1167095#post1167095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that if you're building an advanced Essence 4+ Lunar, then you could use Emerald Grasshopper Form for insect totems.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're talking about 2e, that was impossible. Essence 4 was very purposefully put out of typical Lunar chargen's reach, and besides, EGF never specified that it expanded the choice of Lunar totems - only Humble Mouse Shape and Towering Beast Form ever had that text, suggesting strongly that 2e was more comfortable with allowing Lunars to turn into demons than it was with letting them naturally turn into most arthropods. Such was the way of 2e, and it is now another roadmap of where not to go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Next group!<br /> <br /> Robber fly, poison dart frog, koi, and giant tortoise.<br /> <br /> I'll be amazed if anyone knows that first one without looking it up. </div> </div> </div>Can you name the world's only actually poisonous snake without looking it up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T00:14:58-08:00","id":1167235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1167070-odd-lunar-concepts?p=1167091#post1167091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not even really a challenge. Locusts, especially if they're large enough to qualify as even a small Lunar totem, are ravenous destroyers of crops and vegetation. The character could be driving the Realm off with appetite alone, since it can't gain a foothold where it can't trust its food supplies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Locust Crusade remastered?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>She/Her pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12975-zealot_vedas","name":"Zealot_Vedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12975_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T04:33:29-08:00","id":1167262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1167070-odd-lunar-concepts?p=1167220#post1167220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you're talking about 2e, that was impossible. Essence 4 was very purposefully put out of typical Lunar chargen's reach, and besides, EGF never specified that it expanded the choice of Lunar totems - only Humble Mouse Shape and Towering Beast Form ever had that text, suggesting strongly that 2e was more comfortable with allowing Lunars to turn into demons than it was with letting them naturally turn into most arthropods. Such was the way of 2e, and it is now another roadmap of where not to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>I misremembered EGF, it only needs Essence 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Teller of Tales, and the Weaver of Dreams<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14qUE6JyfwtXyd8SMY5gSJ_vvUZPCvGDZiIbBk19QPiU/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Behold! My 2e characters.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13327-voyd211","name":"Voyd211","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13327_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T07:28:22-08:00","id":1167295,"title":"","content":"Lobster is a sailing one, I'm imagine with incredible strength, but also shocking longevity or the like. An Old sea captain who exalted at like, 70. Full moon.<br /> Pelicans....hm. Oddly, one of the big things I remeber about Pelicans (apart from being really big) isthe old notion that they cut themselves and fed children with their blood. A lunar who enjoys the sea and scattering ships like fish comes to mind. <br /> ...I'm making a lunar circle pirate crew","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T09:49:45-08:00","id":1167339,"title":"","content":"For the Robber Fly, an aggressive assassin of either the Raksha or the Exalted serving the Realm.<br /> <br /> For Bee, I am guessing a honey bee, and this one I'd propose a Lunar architect that has an interest in building societies on the edge of the Wyld to harvest it's resources, possibly building a multitude of Manses, and to extend the edges Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":1813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","user":"grimjaws","date":". 12-13-2017, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T11:25:59-08:00","id":1167363,"title":"","content":"I've got a few Lunars, two of which are in <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14qUE6JyfwtXyd8SMY5gSJ_vvUZPCvGDZiIbBk19QPiU/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">my character doc</a>: a direwolf and a deep-sea angler. The anglerfish was the most random plotbunny I had, and I just ran with it.<br /> <br /> I have a third Lunar character (I just haven't updated his stats) whose spirit shape is a crow, and he's the character most explicitly based on myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Teller of Tales, and the Weaver of Dreams<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14qUE6JyfwtXyd8SMY5gSJ_vvUZPCvGDZiIbBk19QPiU/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Behold! My 2e characters.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13327-voyd211","name":"Voyd211","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13327_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T11:48:32-08:00","id":1167371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voyd211</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1167070-odd-lunar-concepts?p=1167262#post1167262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I misremembered EGF, it only needs Essence 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point about it not actually mentioning an expansion of totem choices still stands. That was why you also couldn't have anything other than unmutated natural animals as spirit shapes; even if you got your hands on Green Sun Child at chargen through flaws, you still couldn't choose to have a demon as a totem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I've got a few Lunars, two of which are in </span></span></span><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14qUE6JyfwtXyd8SMY5gSJ_vvUZPCvGDZiIbBk19QPiU/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">my character doc</a><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: a direwolf and a deep-sea angler. The anglerfish was the most random plotbunny I had, and I just ran with it.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Ah, the dire wolf - the slow-running Leeroy Jenkins of canids, quick to run into the tar pits after mired mammoths. It might be a good time to note that they were only the size of large dog, and would have been dwarfed by the largest of large dogs. Even AD&amp;D, which gave us the alleged horse-size of the animal, originally had them as merely size M in the 1e MM; whatever oddity happened in 2e that spread is not reflective of fossil fauna. It's just a crude copy of the worg, which was described as an overly large &quot;neo dire wolf&quot; in its original MM entry, its size one of the ways in which it was differentiated from actual dire wolves.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> The deep sea angler could be a twist on a woman from Coral, given the way reproduction works for anglerfish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T12:05:34-08:00","id":1167379,"title":"","content":"She is a woman from Coral; a former prostitute, to be precise. A bunch of goons killed the establishment's owner and planned on making the girls their playthings; her sudden overdose on stab-crazy, her Exaltation, and the fact that she suddenly sprouted foot-long fangs changed the survivors' minds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Teller of Tales, and the Weaver of Dreams<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14qUE6JyfwtXyd8SMY5gSJ_vvUZPCvGDZiIbBk19QPiU/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Behold! My 2e characters.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13327-voyd211","name":"Voyd211","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13327_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T04:22:47-08:00","id":1167565,"title":"","content":"Clanking Locust should be the first Lunar Exaltation following in the wake of the Autobots - themed after the whirling clockwork beasties and monsters that they bring with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T08:45:52-08:00","id":1168809,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Mountain Goat</b></u><br /> It is said among the Urut'Al that the Jagged Peaks once rose from the ground with pride and pierced into the vault of the snowy winds. Contained within the vault were thousands of hungry spirits of immaterial, flensing cold. The tribes of the region say those spirits now prowl the mountains when the sun sinks low; that they rally for war against the rest of the world in the waning months of winter and march in the guise of powerful blizzards - in truth, the mountains are entirely mundane albeit very cold and windy. To be banished to the mountains is a death sentence the Urut'Al tribe of the North reserve for the only unforgivable crime of their tribe: being born outside of wedlock. However, this death sentence has become far less lethal in recent years as the No-Moon Kalden Meadhorn has made this range his escape from the Wyld Hunt. A compassionate man, Kald could not stand to leave these dispossessed to death from exposure and so adopted them as he found them. With no milk to give the infants, he instead let them suckle from his own goat blood and they were changed by it. Now, the mountain teems with faun-children; human-like creatures with the legs and horns of goats. These children revere their Goatfather as a savior and a living god and repay the gift of blood and life with prayer. With only a distracted sorcerer as a parent, these children grew mostly in the wild and know nothing of civilization. With little in the way of guiding morals, they're nasty, brutish things to all but their parent - Kald has no idea about how they have been attacking passerby's and becoming more and more warlike. Kald does not know what his next move is, but he knows the Wyld hunt gave up their search years ago and he feels the limitations of his current environment tightening around his desire for sorcerous knowledge. He will leave these mountains soon and plans to have his adopted children march with him - woe upon the lands they pass through.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Locust</u></b><br /> Ledaal Kisha didn't exalt as a Dragon Blooded and it disappointed everybody but her. She, you see, had become obsessed with the intrigues of Dynastic society and found them to be the highest drama imaginable. Had she exalted, she would have been forced onto the stage and that was a terrible vantage point to watch the show. Instead, she sought a front row seat just outside of the action. With canny and grace she insinuated herself into some of the most dangerous and decadent coteries within the Dynast enclaves and watched as murderous interpersonal conflict spilled blood in front of her. Intrigued by her survival amid these dangerous circles and the nature of her curious hunt, the Changing Lady quietly bestowed the exaltation of the Trickster's Moon upon Kisha. Since then, Kisha has taken the form of all manner of insects to be a literal fly upon the wall within the courts of the Dragon Blooded of the Threshold. Though her mind holds a wealth of blackmail and secrets that could undo swaths of the Realm, she has no intention to use them - not all at once anyway. Instead, she uses her arsenal of &quot;Dramatic Twists&quot; and &quot;Shocking Revelations&quot; to stir the drama back into action when things start to bore her. The Silver Pact lusts after her arsenal of Realm secrets and has made overtures to recruit her. She has rebuffed all of these offers concretely and many of them lethally. The Silver Pact, as she sees it, wishes to cancel her favorite stage production and that simply cannot stand. When threats to the Realm enter into her attention, she quickly raises the alarm or resolves them herself. At the same time, she is also a dangerous and typically entirely unnoticed enemy to those seeking to reform and improve the Realm. It's current state of vicious, semi-sustainable dysfunction entertains her greatly and Bronze Caste idealists trying to turn the Realm into something better also perish beneath her silver knife with some regularity. The only positive or negative change to the Realm she shall permit must come from within and - most of all - it had better be interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":5526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","user":"Steamfunk","date":". 12-19-2017, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T09:13:33-08:00","id":1168813,"title":"","content":"I see the Koi Lunar as a Changing Moon, a graceful dancer (and swimmer, obviously) who looks like she's floating through the air. Likely a Dreaming Pearl Stylist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}